68 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 29 0 R
/E (The talk indicated that problem solving can draw on several modes of thinking. Critical thinking is defined as reasonable, reflective, responsible, and skilful thinking that focuses on deciding what to believe or do, in pursuit of relevant and reliable knowledge about the world \(Othman, 2026\). Creative thinking involves solving problems by generating alternative solutions, perspectives, and possibilities. Mathematical thinking entails decomposing complex problems into simpler components and analysing data through observation, pattern recognition, and generalisation. Scientific thinking involves formulating hypotheses, conducting experiments, collecting data, constructing graphs, and drawing conclusions. Higher-order thinking skills \(HOTS\) require individuals to analyse, evaluate, and synthesise information in order to produce new solutions to complex problems. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
69 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 29 0 R
/E (Problem: One of the most common problems faced by university students is the difficulty of finding available parking spaces without a modern system. Students spend a lot of time searching for parking, especially during peak hour.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
70 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 29 0 R
/E (Analysis: Collect and analyse parking data, such as the number of available spaces, vehicle arrival times and peak hours. This information helps to develop a more effective parking management system that saves time and reduces traffic congestion.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
71 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 29 0 R
/E (Solution: Developing a Smart University Parking Application. This application allows students to check real-time parking availability, receive alternative parking suggestions and navigate to available parking areas.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
72 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 29 0 R
/E (Possibilities: Develop an AI-Driven predictive parking system that analyze real-time occupancy patterns and predict peak demand times for better traffic flow management. Students can avoid overcrowded parking areas.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
73 0 obj
<<
